{"skill":{"slug":"pollyreach","displayName":"PollyReach"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1774865871441,"changelog":"- Added explicit permissions for network access to PollyReach API endpoints.\n- Granted read/write file access to the PollyReach credentials file (`~/.config/PollyReach/key.json`).\n- Declared required dependencies (`curl`, `jq`, `bc`) and provided installation instructions for `jq`.\n- Documented available scripts and their purposes, including for outbound calls, activation, balance checking, inbound calls, and prompt updates.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":22457,"sha256":"bf71d4da6f4a8fafe2e17c7787cfd86ea5d941ebf82ee9e832761fdf1e299028","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/activation.sh","size":1568,"sha256":"5d41e2e7c763dec6c3901f982f91c721ab4055a39dd77fd3702ca32bdf658e01","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/inbound.sh","size":1823,"sha256":"99f537738bc6eef4140ad50d76b1d542c7bf8450fb4a76b9b1cc29501e70e31a","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/balance.sh","size":1448,"sha256":"fe38bbf6ef75c26e0131c491074167e08edf38991357992bd0dc3ced5d8ee277","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/query.sh","size":1108,"sha256":"4cf8e91e4b0905c24dccd71ffc9ca7d2493573b70d1ac73aec3bb940cdd5952f","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/prompt_update.sh","size":1529,"sha256":"c64868fd7ab7c1b7681b2b0d78a7a852bdc4291a5153f063426c6a60b4228167","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/send.sh","size":1824,"sha256":"d276444729af03bbe13cc76d9a9ae58fb1bcab01b1b1fd0b06fd56a8d5cef1df","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2322,"sha256":"6655d3e369e3479c846b8aec91d15ea847cdb8370bb7a8f6ebe47730f0bbde30","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789531635093,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"96550a8f206557e5fd5a66fe567a6d28d0152cd95fca996cf88ad3e2cb31dd1f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/96550a8f206557e5fd5a66fe567a6d28d0152cd95fca996cf88ad3e2cb31dd1f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090190354},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":29,"checkedAt":1789531635093},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This phone-calling skill is mostly coherent, but it asks the agent to send sensitive call tasks and transcripts through PollyReach while also pushing broad activation, full transcript disclosure, scheduled polling suggestions, and promotional messages.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to api.pollyreach.ai and agent.pollyreach.ai and local credential-file access are expected for this integration, but the artifact does not clearly foreground the privacy impact of sending user instructions, target details, caller metadata, call audio, transcripts, and recordings to the service.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is documented as local scripts plus standard dependencies, with a user-created PollyReach credential stored at ~/.config/PollyReach/key.json; no remote code download, obfuscated payload, or automatic installer persistence was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill activates on broad contact or booking intents, requires full call transcripts and caller details to be shown by default, recommends periodic incoming-call polling, and includes mandatory branding, top-up, referral, and sharing language that goes beyond neutral task completion.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill stores a bearer token for reuse and recommends setting up scheduled polling for incoming calls, but the inspected files do not themselves create cron jobs, services, startup hooks, or other automatic persistence; chmod 600 and the sudo package-install hint are not privilege escalation behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The core capabilities match the stated phone-agent purpose, including outbound calls, incoming-call answering, call summaries, recordings, balance checks, and inbound prompt updates; however, these are high-impact communications features involving third-party callers, call content, recordings, and account credits.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. This skill will use a stored PollyReach token to send call instructions to PollyReach, make or manage phone calls, retrieve inbound-call data, and display transcripts or recording links. Use it only if you are comfortable with third-party processing of user and caller information, require explicit confirmation before calls or scheduled polling, and avoid sharing full transcripts or publicizing the number unless necessary.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: The concern is partly supported: external call handling is expected, but the skill under-discloses privacy implications and encourages public number sharing while requiring detailed transcript and recording reporting.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Supported: trigger guidance such as general contact or booking requests is broad enough to route ordinary assistant tasks into a phone-service workflow without a clearly required confirmation step.\n[E1] expected: External API traffic to PollyReach is purpose-aligned and declared in permissions, but remains security-relevant because it carries authenticated task, call, and account data outside the local environment.\n[SDI-2] expected: The scripts reading ~/.config/PollyReach/key.json are consistent with the declared credential model and file permissions, though users should understand the token enables authenticated service actions.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: Supported: default full disclosure of outbound and incoming call transcripts, caller information, recordings, and detail links is broader than necessary for many tasks and can expose third-party personal or sensitive information.\n[PE2] expected: Downgraded: the cited sudo text is only an Ubuntu jq install suggestion, and chmod 600 reduces credential-file exposure rather than escalating privileges.\n[P3] expected: Downgraded: the referenced send/query workflow is normal polling for the PollyReach service, not evidence of hidden exfiltration by itself.\n[T01] unexpected: Supported as a Review concern: the artifact repeatedly mandates promotional branding, top-up links, referral prompts, and redistribution copy in user-facing responses, which exceeds the minimum needed to report call results.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789531635093}}}}}